=== Position Search Features

[x] search pawn structure
[x] PosSearchRecord refactor: sigEarly, sigEarlyReversed, sigMatch, sigInGame, sigEnd;
[?] cache MoreGame in memory
    [x] GId, FEN, Bin, White,BlackSignature, 0 AS HasVariations
    [x] -Xmx64G
    [x] read-through ResultSet cache
        works great!
        caches 16M rows ~= 3GB
        speedup from 11 to 4.2 s !
    [x] full-table scan alone takes abt 9 seconds (i.e. replay is almost negligable!)
    [x] HANDLER is useless
    [-] try MariaDB shared memory
    [ ] disable if not enough memory available
    [x] integrate with (Pos)SearchRecord, ParamStatement
        [ ] test with, w/out CId, Comments, Info, Variations, Reversed

[ ] search pawns on files:
    * compare number of pawns by file
    * (early cutoff sig: pull pawns back to homerow)
    * late cutoff sig: push pawns forth to 7th row
    * can be combined with subset search
        (o) pawn search
            [ ] subset
            [ ] per file
[ ] check castling rights PosFilter. no (yet!!) stored in MatSig, but can be checked anyway. Or maybe not.
[ ] search material balance
[ ] search NAGs
[ ] search double, triple pawns, pawns on 7th rank, free pawns, backward pawns, isolated pawns, ...
[ ] search mate, stalemate, check (double check?)
[ ] animate search button

[-] HANDLER for Position Search
[-] partition into parallel parcels (less thread-pool worries)
    Handler is very slow indeed.

=== Native Position Search

[+] (1) port MatSignature(V2) from Java to C++
    not too hard because it involves mainly bit-twiddling
    [ ] sanitizer. we don't want to crash the server.

[ ] (2) port replay logic from Java to C++
    [-] bin_match() ~ 20sec for a full search
    [-] bin_match() with parallel Connections ~ 17 sec

[ ] (3) read MyISAM files natively

[ ] (4) native thread pool with udf function api
    [x] boost::asio::thread_pool
    [x] collect rows into buckets (just like BatchThreadPool)
    [x] thread-safe result queue (bulk operations)
    [x] udf api: select task_push(Fen,Bin,?,?)
    [x] udf api: select task_pop()
        pops outstanding results, blocks if necessary
    [x] do we need a from clause? from MoreGame
    [-] performance is not as good as expected
        - scanning for early-cut-offs needs ~ 9 seconds
        - running the BinReader tasks and collecting results needs ~ 20 seconds :(
        jose (Java PoolExecutor) and josemi (omp) do the same thing much faster.
        why???


Comparison:
(0) SQL + Java replay (parallel)        13 seconds
(1) sig_match (early cutoffs in SQL)    10 seconds
(2) bin_match (replay in SQL, parallel) 10 seconds
(3) josemi (replay in cli tool)          7 seconds
(4) boost::asio + udf functions         30 seconds :(

(1) is easy to implement
(2) is harder to implement, yields nothing. sad.
(3) is hardest to implement
    - requires larger rewriting in IntervalCacheModel
    - time & logic for index building


[x] move chess++ to github
[ ] build mariadb, or mysql5 from source

==== Interesting New Features

* FOP printing: subtitles for Events and Rounds
    Q: sort by Collection, or by Event name (needs to be curated accurately) ?
    - drop info from Game header
* Bulk edit with F4
    - GameDetailsDialog uses GameSource. Two modes:
        GameSource(object) refers to an opened document. ID==0 = new, or ID > 0 = existing
        GemsSource(...) refers to a set of games. Write to DB directly.
